{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478643-looking-for-lost-forbidden-lore-in-the-high-umbra","id":1478643,"title":"Looking for lost/forbidden lore in the High Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-11T20:57:12-07:00","id":1478643,"title":"Looking for lost/forbidden lore in the High Umbra","content":"If a Mage, for whatever reason, wanted to help a Tremere/Tzimisce antitribu colleague find a ritual or knowledge of a Path/Way in the Umbra, could he do it? And what are some suggestions on how he and a group of his friends could begin their quest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T06:23:55-07:00","id":1478676,"title":"","content":"It's possible, in so far as in an RPG anything is possible. But even for an RPG that would be a thematic and conceptual big ask. Both the Tzimisce and the Tremere are notorious, albeit for different reasons (the Tzimisce are a bucket of squick and control freak, and the Tremere make Having No Friends a thing). And vampires in general offend the spirits by just being around. So this would require a vampire to find some people, to not think of the people as food, and then to go into the spirit world on an advenure. Yes, it's possible. But there is a lot to set up in advance. <br /> <br /> That said, both the Tzimisce and the Tremere should have access to at least the powers that let them use astral projection to enter the umbra rather than entering it in physical person. Which *might* be a bit easier. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T08:50:09-07:00","id":1478694,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t mean taking the vampire up to the Astral Umbra, simply looking for the spirit or realm that embodies the knowledge and skill of the Way of Earth. And a hypothetical Tzimisce could be a shovelhead that got rescued by a band of Hollow Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-12-2022, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T11:49:31-07:00","id":1478705,"title":"","content":"That should work, though many spirits will still be tetchy around the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T12:22:52-07:00","id":1478708,"title":"","content":"The other great conceptual space for lost information is the Low Umbra. Much less reachable but much more full of fun and interesting complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T20:26:00-07:00","id":1478818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478643-looking-for-lost-forbidden-lore-in-the-high-umbra?p=1478676#post1478676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And vampires in general offend the spirits by just being around. So this would require a vampire to find some people, to not think of the people as food, and then to go into the spirit world on an advenure. Yes, it's possible. But there is a lot to set up in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically middle umbra spirits, and even more specifically gaian or wyld middle umbra spirits. Book of the weaver and wyrm mention that both of their broods can tolerate kindred or even Like them depending on type.<br /> <br /> High Umbral spirits are an entirely different ball game. They don't necessarily have anything to do with werewolf's Triat or even gaia. The high umbra spirit of darth vader is not necessarily going to have an opinion one way or the other about vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478643-looking-for-lost-forbidden-lore-in-the-high-umbra?p=1478676#post1478676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, both the Tzimisce and the Tremere should have access to at least the powers that let them use astral projection to enter the umbra rather than entering it in physical person. Which *might* be a bit easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>^Auspex specifically allows travel along the astral plane, which in both WTA and MTA cosmology is part of the deep/high Umbra(werewolf calls the high umbra the &quot;deep&quot; umbra).<br /> <br /> A vampire that knows where they're going should be able navigate their way into the high umbra even without assistance from the mage. The mage is highly recommended if they want to survive though, as there's few humans blood bags in the spirit world and there's very little that can save them if they accidentally find a spirit that embodies the Idea of the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T01:32:56-07:00","id":1478829,"title":"","content":"Another alternative is for lost knowledge to be in the Shadowlands. Earlier in my current campaign a group of Wraiths recovered a lost ritual from a Heirarchy Library for a Giovanni vampire (they had good reasons so please don't criticise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T16:39:37-07:00","id":1478875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478643-looking-for-lost-forbidden-lore-in-the-high-umbra?p=1478829#post1478829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another alternative is for lost knowledge to be in the Shadowlands. Earlier in my current campaign a group of Wraiths recovered a lost ritual from a Heirarchy Library for a Giovanni vampire (they had good reasons so please don't criticise).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good, but is there perhaps someway they can fish it out of the Sea of Shadows or the Tempest? Doesn't all lost knowledge go there? I think Spectres can pull lost memories out of the Tempest, and Mokole go fishing in the Sea of Shadows for lost knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T12:40:48-07:00","id":1478919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478643-looking-for-lost-forbidden-lore-in-the-high-umbra?p=1478875#post1478875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds good, but is there perhaps someway they can fish it out of the Sea of Shadows or the Tempest? Doesn't all lost knowledge go there? I think Spectres can pull lost memories out of the Tempest, and Mokole go fishing in the Sea of Shadows for lost knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It all depends on what story you're trying to tell. Mine was a heist story so having the maguffin stored in a library was ideal for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}